INT. HALCYON HOUSE — BALCONY — NIGHT

[[SHOT: WIDE — HIGH ANGLE]]
[[ENTER: SLOANE]]
[[WARDROBE: SLOANE: WD-SLOANE-PARTY-GE92]]
[[PROP: PR-SLOANE-CLUTCH: in Sloane's hand]]

The balcony above the ballroom, near midnight. Below, the party has reached the hour when nobody wants to leave. Sloane stands alone at the rail with her clutch, watching it.

[[TIME: 6]]
[[MUSIC: The house band below, warm and a little slower now.]]
[[ENTER: GIDEON]]
[[WARDROBE: GIDEON: WD-GIDEON-SUIT]]

Gideon comes out through the balcony doors and joins her at the rail. He holds out the note. She doesn't take it yet.

[[TIME: 5]]

SLOANE
Who brought it?

GIDEON
Kai.

[[REACTION: SLOANE — Very still.]]

SLOANE
He came here.

GIDEON
Stayed on the steps. Didn't ask to come in.
(beat)
Good waistcoat.

SLOANE
(almost a smile, then not)
He would.

She takes the note.

[[TIME: 2]]
[[HANDOFF: PR-KAI-NOTE: GIDEON → SLOANE]]

She unfolds it and reads.

[[TIME: 3]]
[[SHOT: INSERT — LOCKED OFF]]
[[INSERT: The note in Kai's hand: "Celestine has a vision she never built. She'll never ask. I'm asking."]]
[[HOLD: 3]]

Gideon watches her read it. He waits until she looks up.

[[TIME: 3]]

GIDEON
(gently)
He can't ask. He has no standing. You know that.

SLOANE
I know.

She reads it again. Slowly, all the way through, as if the second time it might say something different. Then she turns it over.

[[TIME: 6]]
[[INSERT: The back of the note: blank.]]

Nothing else. Just the three sentences, and his name nowhere on it.

[[TIME: 3]]
[[HOLD: 2]]

[[SHOT: HIGH ANGLE — OVER THE RAIL]]

Below, the room she built dances on: the pianist and the producer still arguing at the bar, the stranger with a new partner, the orange jacket in the middle of the floor.

[[TIME: 9]]

SLOANE (V.O.)
Every year I tell myself I'll stop deciding who gets what. Every year I'm very good at it.

[[HOLD: 2]]

GIDEON
Want me to send it back?

SLOANE
(a beat)
No.

[[REACTION: GIDEON — He studies her; he expected that answer.]]

GIDEON
Then I'll be downstairs.

He leaves her the balcony.

[[TIME: 3]]
[[EXIT: GIDEON]]

Alone, Sloane folds the note along its creases, tucks it into her clutch, and snaps the clasp shut. She checks her face in the dark glass of the balcony door, finds the hostess again, and goes back down to the party.

[[TIME: 8]]
[[HANDOFF: PR-KAI-NOTE: SLOANE → CLUTCH]]

At the top of the stairs she stops for one breath. The music comes up to meet her. She goes down into it.

[[TIME: 4]]
[[EXIT: SLOANE]]

CUT TO BLACK.
